    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Well, to be elected, you have to be Republican. You have to, it's very difficult for a third party candidate to win now. The last time I remember that, anything giving a raise, I'm dating myself. It was in 1970 when Jim Buckley was elected US Senate and a three-way raise, I think he got 39% of the vote. But as a practical matter, you have to have major parties supported. On the other hand, you're not going to win unless you also have conservative party support. A majority party, whether it's Mike Long, Derek, they've done a great job as far as making that party a real solid, supposed vehicle for the conservative movement. And listen, again, I'm old enough to remember when Republicans always felt they had to move to the left to get elected. The conservative party stopped that. And that's why a great majority of Republicans were elected. I'll like to do with conservative party endorsement. But I think that in doing that, we have to be appealing not just to Republicans and registered conservatives, but also to blue-collar Democrats. You know, these are called Reagan Democrats. Many people, you know, they registered as Democrats because their parents or grandparents identified with, you know, the Democratic Party, whether it was Al Smith or John Kennedy, Ed Koch, that matter. That's not the Democratic Party of today. So we have to make it clear That's the Democratic Party today is a left-wing, extreme group of progressive leftists over there to call themselves their anti-cop against our institutions. We have to make that clear and show that we are not the party of the rich, we're not the party of the country club. So, you know, the party of the guys who play softball on weekends, the mothers who work hard during the day and take care of the kids at night. I mean, the whole thing. We're aware of what it means to be a, we are really the working family's body. And that's the, I know the left is adopted that title. But if you want to look at people who work hard, who are not looking for welfare, not looking for a free ride, and not out there attacking the cops, it's people who share the real values of the Republican conservative bodies.",
