    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "Now, in fact, with Pakistan, they were really bad at the beginning, out of the end, going back to 1998, when the African embassies were attacked, and Bill Clinton launched rocket attacks, which couldn't have killed bin Laden at that time. But the rockets had to go over Pakistan. So Pakistan being a quote unquote ally, we notified Pakistan. So they would know whether you know where these rockets are coming from. And turn out so many of the Pakistani government tipped off bin Laden and bin Laden got away. We got them then. This may all just may not have happened. And then at the end, of the bin Laden era, if you want to call it that, turns out Pakistan was hiding him. And the doctor who cooperated with us and giving us information, as far as I know, is still in jail with Pakistan. So they arrested the guy who, really a patriot, who cooperated to let us know where bin Laden was. And Pakistan's response was to arrest him. As far as I know, no, I've been out of Congress, but as of the time I left Congress, he was still in jail.",
