    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51684.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 44,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, that's by the way, when any vote comes up. which is indicative whether or not you pro or anti-Israel, maybe you get one Republican vote. It's usually some guy who just has a opposition to foreign aid. It's something to do with Israel. But Democrats, they identify, I guess, with these radical insurgents. It's not all Democrats, but it's not the way it used to be over the years. It used to be democrats republicans stood as warned when it came to israel right now it's uh i think part of it is uh i'll say this they're being consistent i mean they uh uh well you're showing you're the aoc types or someone like uh you know an omar out in uh minnesota you're talking about uh to leave in Michigan. I mean, these people are pro-Palestinian. They believe in these insurgency movements. And also Israel is, in many ways, everything they're opposed to. It's basically a capitalist country. It's very democratic, very pro-military. and allies with the United States. So those are all negatives in the eyes of, you know, the hardcore left in the Democratic Party, which used to be three or four people you were talking about. Now it's getting stronger and stronger. Really is that left wing in the Democratic Party. I was just talking to a friend of mine the other day, Henry Quayo, a Democrat along the border in Texas. And he's had now two massive primaries against him launched by AOC. And of course, millions and millions and millions of dollars. And looks at if he's won this time, But they're after him because he's pro-life, because he's basically pro-American, and because he's willing to work with Republicans, and also because he wants strong border security. And they just feel it's wrong for Democrats to be saying anything at all that's against open immigration.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
