    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51684.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "So I did a lot of media when I was in Congress. And the reason I did that was a lot of it was very pragmatic. The only real media outlet in Nassau County or in Suffolk County was Newsday. They basically had a monopoly. Post the Daily News could be good, but that mainly city-oriented. Newsday was the one that covered Nassau and Suffolk every day, every minute. And quite frankly, I had a long-term benefit with Newsday. So I didn't want my whole political career and political life and my message controlled by a news day. So I did every bit of free media that I could, a lot of radio, a lot of television, I used to go on, again, certainly on ABC with the IMS and Ernie and Sid, John Gambling, all those type shows, and also other stations in New York too. And I did a lot of television. So I never thought about actually having, you know, being on radio as a job, But in my, near the end, John Cashman Teetees said to me, I'd like to talk to you when you're out of Congress. So anyway, we basically, he wanted to make WABC. He wanted to bring it back. It was really on its death store stuff there for a",
